{%- comment -%}
  Resolve a cart-goal spend threshold for the active presentment currency.

  Cart-goal thresholds are stored in MAJOR currency units in the shop's primary
  currency (e.g. "90" = $90.00). But cart.total_price (Liquid) and the AJAX cart
  total (cart-drawer.js) are in the customer's PRESENTMENT currency minor units.
  Comparing the raw stored number against a presentment-currency total means a
  weak-currency market (PLN, CZK) clears a USD-denominated gate far too cheaply
  — e.g. a "$90" makeup-bag goal becomes "90 zł" (~$23) in Poland.

  This snippet picks the right threshold for the active currency from a
  per-market override list, falling back to the base (shop-currency) value.

  Params:
    base      - settings.cart_goal_N_threshold  (major units, shop primary currency)
    overrides - settings.cart_goal_N_currency_overrides
                ("CODE:amount" pairs in each currency's own major units,
                 comma-separated, e.g. "PLN:360, CZK:2100, EUR:85")
    currency  - active presentment currency ISO code (e.g. cart.currency.iso_code)

  Output: the resolved threshold in MAJOR units of the active currency.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign _result = base | default: 0
  assign _overrides = overrides | default: ''
  assign _currency = currency | default: '' | upcase

  if _overrides != '' and _currency != ''
    assign _pairs = _overrides | split: ','
    for _pair in _pairs
      assign _kv = _pair | split: ':'
      if _kv.size < 2
        continue
      endif
      assign _code = _kv[0] | strip | upcase
      assign _amt = _kv[1] | strip
      if _code == _currency and _amt != ''
        assign _result = _amt
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
{{- _result -}}
